title: 'hrmp: fix request count and system-channel refund when offboarding drops open channel requests'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    Two fixes in the cleanup of open channel requests whose sender or recipient offboards:

    - The sender's open request count is decremented when only the recipient offboards. Before,
      the removed request kept counting against the sender's outbound channel limit for good.
    - No recipient deposit is given back for a confirmed request with or amongst the system, since
      `accept_open_channel` takes none for those. Before, the cleanup unreserved
      `hrmp_recipient_deposit` from the counterparty's account anyway, freeing reserves that back
      its other channels.

    The weight of the request cleanup is benchmarked with confirmed requests, which is now the
    worst case.

    No storage, API or configuration change. Request counts already leaked by earlier versions are
    not touched.
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: patch
